---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Summary from '../components/Summary.astro';
import Divider from '../components/Divider.astro';
---
<Base title={"Telehealth Therapy in Utah | Online Counseling  | Tangible Therapy"} description={"Online therapy for anyone in Utah. The same expert care from our Provo, Orem & Sandy offices—from wherever you are. Book a free 15-min consult."}>
<section class="sec t-black h-medium has-bg has-div" style="--divh:6vw">
<div class="sec-bg"><img src="/images/tangible-13-69dc0b.jpg" alt="" style="object-position:24% 2%" loading="eager"><div class="sec-ov" style="opacity:0.4"></div></div><div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:9;--mrows:9">
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:1/7/8/21;--m:1/2/7/10"><div class="rte"><h1 class="ta-center">Telehealth Therapy Across Utah</h1><p class="ta-center">Expert therapy from wherever you are; no commute, no waiting room, just real support.</p></div></div>
  <div class="b b-button jc" style="--d:8/11/10/17;--m:7/3/9/9;--dz:4;--mz:4"><div class="btn-wrap ta-center"><a class="btn btn-primary btn-medium btn-full" href="/contact">Book Your First Session</a></div></div>
</div>
</div>
<Divider type="wavy" height={6} width={100} fill="#fff" /></section>

<section class="sec t-bright-inverse h-small">
<div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:13;--mrows:20">
  <div class="b b-image jc" style="--d:2/15/13/26;--m:13/2/20/10;--dz:4;--mz:4"><figure class="img fill" style="--r:50px"><img src="/images/man-telehealth-therapy-936e08.jpg" alt="A man with a green shirt and dark hair sits in front of a computer in an office while doing telehealth therapy at Tangible in Orem, Provo and Sandy Utah. The room is warmly lit and decorated with plants" width="1536" height="1024" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:3/2/5/12;--m:1/2/4/10;--dz:2;--mz:2"><div class="rte"><h3>Same Care, More Access</h3></div></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:5/2/12/12;--m:4/2/13/10;--dz:3;--mz:3"><div class="rte"><p>You shouldn’t have to rearrange your entire day to take care of your mental health. Telehealth therapy gives you access to the same licensed therapists, the same evidence-based approaches, and the same quality of care our clients receive in our Provo, Orem, and Sandy offices, from your couch, your car on lunch break, or wherever you feel comfortable.</p><p>Whether you’re in Salt Lake City, St. George, Logan, or a small town in between, if you’re in Utah, we can work together.</p></div></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="sec t-black h-small">
<div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:15;--mrows:23">
  <div class="b b-image jc" style="--d:2/2/14/13;--m:16/2/24/10;--dz:4;--mz:4"><figure class="img fill" style="--r:50px"><img src="/images/woman-telehealth-d20e95.jpg" alt="A woman with a tan shirt and dark hair sits in front of a computer in an office while doing telehealth therapy at Tangible in Orem, Provo and Sandy Utah. The room is warmly lit and decorated with plants" width="1122" height="1402" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:3/15/6/25;--m:2/2/5/10;--dz:2;--mz:2"><div class="rte"><h3>How Telehealth Works at Tangible</h3></div></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:6/15/12/25;--m:5/2/16/10;--dz:3;--mz:3"><div class="rte"><p>It’s simple. You book a session, we send you a secure video link, and you connect with your therapist at your scheduled time. No apps to download, no complicated setup. Just click and you’re in.</p><p>Sessions are 50 minutes, just like in-person. Your therapist uses the same tools and techniques: ACT, EMDR, IFS, Gottman, somatic approaches, adapted thoughtfully for a virtual setting. Many of our clients are surprised by how natural it feels.</p></div></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="sec t-bright-inverse h-small">
<div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:19;--mrows:23">
  <div class="b b-image jc" style="--d:2/15/18/26;--m:17/2/24/10;--dz:4;--mz:4"><figure class="img fill" style="--r:50px"><img src="/images/tangible-30-3272eb.jpg" alt="A black female therapist with a green shirt and dark hair sits in front of a computer in an office while doing telehealth therapy with a client at Tangible in Utah. The room is warmly lit and decorated with plants" width="2500" height="1603" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:3/2/5/12;--m:1/2/4/10;--dz:2;--mz:2"><div class="rte"><h3>Who Telehealth is Right For</h3></div></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:5/2/19/12;--m:4/2/16/10;--dz:3;--mz:3"><div class="rte"><p>Telehealth works well for most of what we treat. If you’re dealing with anxiety, depression, OCD, trauma, relationship issues, faith transitions, or just feeling stuck, virtual sessions can be every bit as effective as sitting in our office.</p><p>Online therapy is especially helpful if you:</p><ul><li><p>Live outside Utah County but want access to specialized care</p></li><li><p>Have a demanding schedule or limited childcare</p></li><li><p>Feel more comfortable opening up from home</p></li><li><p>Are a college student away from your hometown therapist</p></li><li><p>Experience social anxiety that makes in-person visits harder</p></li><li><p>Need couples counseling but can’t coordinate schedules to come in together</p></li></ul><p>If your situation calls for in-person care, we’ll let you know. But for most people, telehealth is a great fit — and research consistently backs that up.</p></div></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="sec t-black h-small">
<div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:20;--mrows:27">
  <div class="b b-image jc" style="--d:2/2/18/13;--m:19/2/27/10;--dz:4;--mz:4"><figure class="img fill" style="--r:50px"><img src="/images/healing-via-telehealth-ae2b0d.jpg" alt="Woman engages in virtual therapy via telehealth sitting on a comfy chair and using a laptop" width="1890" height="2363" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:3/15/6/25;--m:1/2/4/10;--dz:2;--mz:2"><div class="rte"><h3>What We Treat Through Telehealth</h3></div></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:6/15/19/25;--m:4/2/19/10;--dz:3;--mz:3"><div class="rte"><p>Our telehealth therapists work with the same range of concerns as our in-office team:</p><ul><li><p><a href="/anxiety-therapy">Anxiety and panic attacks</a></p></li><li><p><a href="/depression-therapy">Depression and low motivation</a></p></li><li><p><a href="/ocd-treatment">OCD and intrusive thoughts (including ERP therapy)</a></p></li><li><p><a href="/trauma-therapy">Trauma and PTSD</a></p></li><li><p><a href="/emdr-therapy">EMDR therapy</a></p></li><li><p><a href="/couples-counseling">Couples and relationship issues</a></p></li><li><p><a href="/faith-transition-therapy">Faith transitions and religious trauma</a></p></li><li><p><a href="/therapy-for-teens">Teen therapy</a> (ages 13+)</p></li><li><p><a href="/adhd-therapy">ADHD</a></p></li><li><p><a href="/grief-therapy">Grief and loss</a></p></li><li><p><a href="/counseling">Life transitions and stress</a></p></li></ul></div></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="sec t-black h-small">
<div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:13;--mrows:11">
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:2/6/4/22;--m:1/2/4/10"><div class="rte"><h2 class="ta-center">Let’s get started</h2></div></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:4/5/11/23;--m:3/2/9/10;--dz:2;--mz:2"><div class="rte"><p class="lg ta-center">Getting started is easy. Book a free 15-minute consultation, and we’ll match you with a therapist who fits your needs: whether that’s someone who specializes in trauma, OCD, couples work, or anything else. From there, your first full session can happen as early as this week.</p><p class="lg ta-center">Telehealth sessions are $115 for cash pay, and we work with most major insurance providers. Our client’s average copay is typically around $25.</p></div></div>
  <div class="b b-button jc" style="--d:11/11/13/17;--m:9/2/11/10;--dz:3;--mz:3"><div class="btn-wrap ta-center"><a class="btn btn-primary btn-medium btn-full" href="/contact">Book Your First Appointment</a></div></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="sec t-bright-inverse h-small has-div" style="--divh:6vw">
<div class="sec-in" style="padding-top:6.6vmax;padding-bottom:6.6vmax">
<div class="wrap"><div class="list-title rte"><p>What you’ll get</p></div><ul class="ulist ulist-carousel" style="--per:3;--ar:3/2;--tfs:calc((2.2 - 1) * var(--fs-unit) + 1rem);--bfs:calc((1.2 - 1) * var(--fs-unit) + 1rem);--cw:75%;--gap:20px"><li class="li"><a class="li-link" href="#" aria-label="✺"></a><div class="li-body"><h3 class="li-title">✺</h3><div class="rte li-desc"><p>50 minutes of focused, one-on-one support with a licensed therapist</p></div></div></li><li class="li"><div class="li-body"><h3 class="li-title">✺</h3><div class="rte li-desc"><p>The same evidence-based approaches used in our offices, CBT, EMDR, IFS, Gottman, and more</p></div></div></li><li class="li"><div class="li-body"><h3 class="li-title">✺</h3><div class="rte li-desc"><p>A secure, HIPAA-compliant video platform with nothing to download</p></div></div></li><li class="li"><div class="li-body"><h3 class="li-title">✺</h3><div class="rte li-desc"><p>Flexible scheduling including evenings to fit your life</p></div></div></li><li class="li"><div class="li-body"><h3 class="li-title">✺</h3><div class="rte li-desc"><p>Access to specialized care no matter where you are in Utah</p></div></div></li><li class="li"><a class="li-link" href="/" aria-label="✺"></a><div class="li-body"><h3 class="li-title">✺</h3><div class="rte li-desc"><p>A therapist matched to your specific needs and goals</p></div></div></li></ul><div class="carousel-nav"><button class="prev" aria-label="Previous"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="28" height="28" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M19 12H5m6-6-6 6 6 6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></button><button class="next" aria-label="Next"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="28" height="28" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14m-6-6 6 6-6 6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></button></div></div>
</div>
<Divider type="wavy" height={6} width={100} fill="#565d57" /></section>

<section class="sec t-light h-medium">
<div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:16;--mrows:7">
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:1/7/3/22;--m:1/2/3/10;--dz:2;--mz:2"><div class="rte"><h2 class="ta-center">Telehealth Therapists</h2></div></div>
  <div class="b b-summary-v2" style="--d:3/5/17/24;--m:3/2/8/10"><Summary kind="team" design="carousel" category="telehealth" limit={9} perRow={3} rounded /></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="sec t-black h-medium">
<div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:14;--mrows:20">
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:2/2/4/26;--m:1/2/4/10"><div class="rte"><h2 class="ta-center"> Frequently asked questions </h2></div></div>
  <div class="b b-accordion" style="--d:6/2/14/13;--m:5/2/13/10"><div class="accordion"><details><summary>Is telehealth therapy as effective as in-person?</summary><div class="rte"><p>For most concerns, yes. Research consistently shows that telehealth therapy produces outcomes comparable to in-person sessions for anxiety, depression, PTSD, OCD, and relationship issues. Some clients actually find they open up more easily from the comfort of their own space.</p></div></details><details><summary>What do I need for a telehealth session?</summary><div class="rte"><p>A reliable internet connection, a device with a camera and microphone, and a private space where you feel comfortable talking openly. That’s it. We send you a secure link before each session; no downloads or accounts needed.</p></div></details><details><summary>Can I do EMDR or couples therapy over telehealth?</summary><div class="rte"><p>Yes to both. EMDR adapts well to virtual sessions; your therapist will guide you through bilateral stimulation using on-screen visuals or audio tones. Couples therapy works well over video too, especially when scheduling in-person sessions is a challenge.</p><p><br/></p></div></details></div></div>
  <div class="b b-accordion" style="--d:6/15/15/26;--m:13/2/21/10;--dz:2;--mz:2"><div class="accordion"><details><summary>Do you accept insurance for telehealth?</summary><div class="rte"><p>Yes. We accept most major insurance plans for telehealth sessions, and coverage works the same as in-person visits. Cash pay is $115 per session, and the average insurance copay is around $25. We’ll verify your benefits before your first appointment.</p></div></details><details><summary>I live outside of Utah County. Can I still see your therapists?</summary><div class="rte"><p>Absolutely. Our therapists are licensed in Utah, so we can see anyone located anywhere in the state: Salt Lake, Park City, Cedar City, Ogden, you name it. You get the same specialized care without the drive to Provo or Orem.</p></div></details><details><summary>What if I want to switch between telehealth and in-person?</summary><div class="rte"><p>That’s completely fine. Many of our clients do a mix; coming into our Provo, Orem, or Sandy office when it works and switching to video when it doesn’t. Your therapist stays the same either way.</p></div></details></div></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</Base>
